From 8a6173c18ad43fa62433e6f67acc541f70336c1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pierre Wielders <pierre@wielders.net>
Date: Mon, 21 Jun 2021 14:01:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Increase buffer size of COMRPC messages

Cherry-picked from R4

- c1a553eb45bf278b5fb72809bccd0663dabfe8dd

[WARNINGS] Warnings from the windows build resolved. (#623)

These warnings include uninitialized variables during construction.
Potential leaks (and than a crash, due to nullptr access) if the realloc would *not* allocate a new buffer that is big enough..

- 119af9fd2d23ecd61a752c139d201923bbd368b7
[FRAME] Extend the functionality of the Frame template. (#840)

* [FRAME] Extend the functionality of the Frame template.
Sometimes the ordering in a binary serialzed frame is LSB, sometimes it is MSB. Allow the template to
cope with both situations, the default is MSB as that was as it was used sofar.
Also sometimes we only need to work with very small frames <255 bytes. using the the uint16_t for maintaining
location and size is a bit of overkill. Maybe in the future we would like to enlarge the 64Kb boundary to
4Gb, and the variables than need to be uint32_t :-)
Make the variable sizes for creating the buffers a template parameter, again making the default equal to
what it was.

* [FRAME] Update after review.

[WINDOWS] Make new Time compile with less warnings on Windows.

Co-authored-by: MFransen69 <39826971+MFransen69@users.noreply.github.com>

- 3246752780ea56c98d930e18ebf15ecd55a73e54

[COMRPC] Enlarge the buffer in which we hold the COMRPC message to 32 bits. Now it can grow beyond the 64Kb. (#1116)
